 \subsection{Initialization and adaptation}\label{app:initialization}
 The encoder and waveform decoder are initialized from DGF weights identified in the accompanying manifest. The associated bank contains 10,000 auxiliary single-series simulations with source total mass uniform over $[10^5,10^6]\,M_\odot$, mass ratio over $[0.5,0.8]$ and redshift over $[4,6]$. The associated training configuration combines pointwise squared and absolute errors with equal weights and unit mask weight. The physical training, validation and test populations use the disjoint seed ranges given above. Physical $A/E$ adaptation uses 12,000 training sources with 33-s gaps and objective $\mathcal M_{AE}+0.5E_S+0.5E_{\rm time,gap}$, then 60,000 sources for joint-channel and physical-frequency adaptation with an additional Hann-windowed penalty.
